files.description:
evaluations.csv: contains the evaluations provided by the participants for each scenario. More specifically, each participant evaluated six group configurations in a specific combination of the control conditions (aggregation strategy and explanation). The columns are: 
- id: automatic generated identifier; 
- agg: between-subject condition assigned to the participant, describing the aggregation strategy used in the scenarios the user evaluated (APP: "Approval Voting", MAJ: "Majority", ADD: "Additive", LMS: "Least Misery", MPL: Most Pleasure", or FAI: "Fairness"); 
- expl: between-subject condition assigned to the participant, describing the explanation strategy used in the scenarios the user evaluated  ("NO_EXP": "No Explanation", "EXP": "Basic Explanation"); 
- group_conf: specific group configuration evaluated ("Uniform", "Divergent", "Coalitional_small", "Coalitional_large", "Minority_min", and "Minority_maj");
- ind_fairness: Evaluation of the perceived fairness for the individual of the recommendation, on a 7-point Likert scale (from -3 to 3); 
- ind_consensus: Evaluation of the individual perceived consensus of the recommendation, on a 7-point Likert scale (from -3 to 3); 
- ind_satisfaction: Evaluation of the individual satisfactions of the recommendation, on a 7-point Likert scale (from -3 to 3); 
- grp_fairness: Evaluation of the perceived fairness for the group of the recommendation, on a 7-point Likert scale (from -3 to 3);
- grp_consensus: Evaluation of the group perceived consensus of the recommendation, on a 7-point Likert scale (from -3 to 3); 
- grp_satisfaction: Evaluation of the group satisfactions of the recommendation, on a 7-point Likert scale (from -3 to 3); 
- feedback: general feedback provided for the specific group configuration;
- tot_time: total time for the evaluation of the specific group configuration, in seconds.

